WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:06.150
In Abducted, everyone at the table knows which team you're on.
Except you.

2
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:10.250
Your card faces out in a stand: Human or Alien.

3
00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:12.400
You can read every card but your own,

4
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.300
so the only way to learn your team is to decide who to believe.

5
00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:18.600
Each round, the Town Leader splits the town in two,

6
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.250
and everyone votes on which party goes out searching.

7
00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:25.600
The searchers secretly play Transmit if they think they're an Alien,

8
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.900
or Jam if they think they're Human,

9
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:29.500
and the majority scores.

10
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.400
Guess wrong, and you just scored for the other side.

11
00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:36.000
Then the Lookout sends one searcher to check out the light.

12
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.900
They mix their card with the top of the deck and keep one, blind.

13
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.550
They might come back… different.

14
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.600
So your friends are telling you what you are.

15
00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:49.200
So are your enemies.

16
00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:52.150
And after the next abduction, they might have swapped places.

17
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:57.200
First team to five wins, and you win if the card in your stand is on that team,

18
00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.850
no matter how you played.

19
00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:02.000
Fifty cards and twelve stands in a tuck box.

20
00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:05.350
Five to twelve players, fifteen to twenty-five minutes.

21
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:06.800
Abducted.

22
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.650
Play it in your browser at darrendon.com, or email me for a prototype.

